    {
      "id": "claim_bb692bfc912b48bc8c8d2ef3f101903f",
      "statement": "create_batch selects the tracking branch by checking new_batch.units_remaining is None (None means weight-tracked); a payload supplying both quantity fields would pass validation and produce an IN movement mirroring the grams value, so the exactly-one-quantity rule is a UI-enforced convention, not a server-side XOR invariant.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://main.py#L46-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e57ce23b27e935c59a6b223089084d5472bc30486527b56c4b2399cc4fa989b8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_25b9633a2cc849b6a61fc5e541b02f5c",
      "statement": "Both consumption endpoints (POST /scan and POST /deduct) select batches with a shared FEFO eligibility filter: variety_id match, expiry_date >= date.today() (inclusive on expiry day), positive remaining stock, ordered by expiry_date ascending, with .with_for_update() row locks so concurrent scans serialize on the same batch rows.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://main.py#L152-L215",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3fc9b51fa7bda6d1ce88267dad91503365e893222d0610813872ca7f1f3fa6a0:"
        },
        {
