        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7165068ecb3745b5afe785e35e3870da",
      "statement": "In the /scan weight branch, the handler drains batches in expiry order writing one OUT/SALE movement per batch touched (barcode=scan.barcode), then records any uncovered shortfall as one extra OUT/SALE movement with batch_id=None so movements always sum to the full package_size_grams; the response carries stock_shortfall and status completed (shortfall 0) or stock_mismatch. A weight product without package_size_grams is a 400.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://main.py#L85-L132",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2f7415d66040843c20ecb6ca5c4746d9c7ae081f92472338a2024640ac21be9d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0e56c69f70974bfaac604e953d96216d",
      "statement": "In the /scan unit branch, exactly one unit is taken from the first non-expired batch with units_remaining > 0 (a .first() query, not a loop), one OUT/SALE movement with grams=1 is written, and no batch yields 404 'Batch not found'; the response is always units_removed=1, status completed with no shortfall concept.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://main.py#L133-L150",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5c1effb02d66e551c0511ce6891ce52f3f1589759b29a879c7e08d4461e58581:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_42d7660cbcd9410ba818e60daac432c7",
      "statement": "POST /deduct applies the same FEFO chain for both tracking types with barcode=None SALE/OUT movements: the weight branch subtracts deduct.grams across batches and always reports completed without shortfall tracking, while the unit branch chains across batches with spillover, records grams=units_removed, and reports stock_mismatch when a remainder is uncovered; DeductModal submits variety_id plus the tracking-appropriate quantity.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/src/DeductModal.jsx#L17-L61",
